            <span class="nm">in_valid</span><span class="val">1</span>
          </div>
          <div class="as-row child">
            <span class="ic" style="color:var(--text-2)"><svg width="13" height="13" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"></circle><path d="m8.4 12.3 2.4 2.4 4.7-5.4"></path></svg></span>
            <span class="nm">in_ready</span><span class="val">0</span>
          </div>
          <div class="as-row child">
            <span class="ic"><svg width="13" height="13" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M3 12h4l2.5-7 4 14 2.5-7H21"></path></svg></span>
            <span class="nm">in_data[7:0]</span><span class="vpill" style="--pc:var(--pink)">A3</span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- ungrouped -->
        <div class="as-row"><span class="pin" style="background:var(--bus)"></span><span class="ic"><svg width="13" height="13" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 8h6l2 8 2-12h4"></path></svg></span><span class="nm">state[1:0]</span><span class="vpill" style="--pc:var(--bus)">BUSY</span></div>
        <div class="as-row"><span class="pin" style="background:var(--warn)"></span><span class="ic"><svg width="13" height="13" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M3 12h4l2.5-7 4 14 2.5-7H21"></path></svg></span><span class="nm">fifo_level[3:0]</span><span class="val">2</span></div>
        <div class="as-row"><span class="pin" style="background:#4FD2BD"></span><span class="ic" style="color:#4FD2BD"><svg width="13" height="13" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M3 9.5c2.2-2.6 4.4 1 6.5-1s4.3-3.6 6.5-1"></path><path d="M3 15c2.2-2.6 4.4 1 6.5-1s4.3-3.6 6.5-1"></path></svg></span><span class="nm">stall</span><span class="dtag">derived</span><span class="val">1</span></div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="copy">
      <div class="sec-kicker">// ORGANIZATION</div>
      <h2>Group signals the way you think.</h2>
      <p>Bundle a handshake, a bus, or a valid/data pair into a group, then move, color or collapse them as one. Riptide can read the hierarchy and naming patterns to assign group colors automatically, so you spend less time housekeeping.</p>
      <ul class="feat-list">
        <li><span class="pin" style="background:var(--clk)"></span><div><strong>Logical groups</strong><span>Group related signals, color them, collapse them together.</span></div></li>
        <li><span class="pin" style="background:#4FD2BD"></span><div><strong>Auto group detection</strong><span>Hierarchy and name patterns seed groups and colors for you.</span></div></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- HANDOFF / SIDECAR -->
<section class="section band" id="handoff">
  <div class="wrap split">
    <div class="copy">
      <div class="sec-kicker">// HANDOFF</div>
      <h2>Hand over the bug, not the trace.</h2>
      <p>Riptide keeps viewer state in a small JSON <span class="mono">sidecar</span> beside the trace — which signals, what order, colors, cursor, markers, zoom. It's tied to signal names, so the same sidecar opens against any run of the design. Drop a VCD and a sidecar from a failing CI job into review: the reviewer double-clicks and lands on the failure window, the right signals already up.</p>
      <ul class="feat-list">
        <li><span class="pin" style="background:var(--accent)"></span><div><strong>Portable across runs</strong><span>Tied to signal names, so the same view opens against any run of the design.</span></div></li>
        <li><span class="pin" style="background:var(--bus)"></span><div><strong>Scriptable for CI</strong><span>A script writes the <span class="mono">view</span> section; Riptide fills the rest in.</span></div></li>
        <li><span class="pin" style="background:var(--ok)"></span><div><strong>Autosaved, no projects</strong><span>Every change is written back — delete the file to open fresh.</span></div></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="codecard">
      <div class="top"><span class="dot"></span> keysched.sidecar.json</div>
      <pre><span class="c-key">"view"</span>: {
  <span class="c-key">"time"</span>: { <span class="c-key">"start"</span>: <span class="c-num">88</span>, <span class="c-key">"end"</span>: <span class="c-num">132</span>, <span class="c-key">"cursor"</span>: <span class="c-num">104.5</span> },
  <span class="c-com">// keyed by path — opens against any run</span>
  <span class="c-key">"signals"</span>: [
    { <span class="c-key">"path"</span>: <span class="c-clk">"top.dec.in_valid"</span> },
    { <span class="c-key">"path"</span>: <span class="c-clk">"top.dec.out_data"</span>, <span class="c-key">"radix"</span>: <span class="c-clk">"hex"</span> }
  ],
  <span class="c-key">"markers"</span>: [
    { <span class="c-key">"t"</span>: <span class="c-num">104</span>, <span class="c-key">"name"</span>: <span class="c-ok">"assert failed"</span> }
  ]
}</pre>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

